    {
      "id": "how-to-judge",
      "group": "method",
      "order": 6,
      "chip": true,
      "q": {
        "zh": "怎么判断一个 AI 功能好不好？",
        "en": "How do you tell whether an AI feature is good?"
      },
      "aliases": {
        "zh": [
          "指标怎么定",
          "怎么评测",
          "评测方法",
          "怎么衡量效果",
          "成功标准",
          "评估"
        ],
        "en": [
          "metrics",
          "how do you evaluate",
          "evaluation method",
          "measure quality",
          "success criteria",
          "assessment"
        ]
      },
      "a": {
        "zh": "先把题目和标准答案写好、冻结，再跑。指标跟着要解决的问题定，例如判对的比例、漏判和误判、每千次的费用，比例都附区间。每改一版就在同一套题上重测，按事先写好的规则决定采不采用。改版记录一共 73 条，没采用的也留着。",
        "en": "Write the test items and answers first, freeze them, then run. The metrics follow the problem, such as the share judged right, misses and false alarms, and cost per thousand, with intervals on every proportion. Each version is re-run on the same items and adopted or not by a rule written beforehand. There are 73 logged changes, dropped versions included."
      },
      "sources": [
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "method",
          "label": {
            "zh": "评测方法",
            "en": "How it is evaluated"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "log",
          "label": {
            "zh": "改版记录",
            "en": "Change log"
          }
        }
      ],
      "related": [
        "iterate-adopt",
        "data-source"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "data-source",
      "group": "method",
      "order": 7,
      "chip": false,
      "q": {
        "zh": "题目和标准答案从哪来？有没有人工标注？",
        "en": "Where do the test items and answers come from? Any human labels?"
      },
      "aliases": {
        "zh": [
          "标准答案",
          "数据从哪来",
          "人工标注",
          "真实数据",
          "真实用户",
          "标注数据",
          "测试集"
        ],
        "en": [
          "ground truth",
          "answer key",
          "human annotation",
          "real data",
          "real users",
          "labelled data",
          "test set"
        ]
      },
      "a": {
        "zh": "多数题目的答案在出题时就定好。另外用到三种外部标准：监管机构和法院对真实广告的结论，公开数据集自带的标注和专家评分（例如 ASAP 点评的方面标签、SummEval），以及 Cairn 里学生用自己的话提的真实问题（经同意公开）。模型裁判校准、标注 Agent 工具箱和 Agent 评测台都没有另做人工评分。",
        "en": "Most items have answers fixed when they were written. Three outside standards are also used: regulator and court decisions on real ads, the labels and expert ratings that ship with public datasets (such as ASAP review aspects and SummEval), and real questions students asked in their own words in Cairn, published with consent. Judge Calibration, the Labelling Agent Kit and Agent Trace Eval collected no human ratings of their own."
      },
      "sources": [
        {
